On 2007-12-31, Carl <carlhnelson@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Dec 31, 5:35 am, Derek Ray <de...@moot.its.only.a.spamtrap.org>
> wrote:
>> PK: New engravings, hallucinatory critters, and epitaphs
>> DR: If you leave bones, your killer will have gone through your possessions
>>     by the time the next person reaches them.
> Is this true even if the deceased drops a scroll of scare monster or
> stops blocking an Elbereth?

The scare monster scroll case is one I'm considering adding; for the
moment, no, your bones will still have been gone through.  WRT Elbereth, 
"killer" is defined in such a way that (because Elbereth is not a 100% 
effective tool in Spork) there should be no way to die to a critter
while standing on Elbereth unless that critter could have ignored
Elbereth in the first place.

>>  -- Demon princes/lords will tend to both take the 'good stuff', and also have
>>     a chance of returning to their home plane.
> This is a nice change; I don't know why you addded it but it takes out
> the insta-kill/insta-win factor associated with a formidable/
> fortuitous bones file.  

Someone hit an early-level Yeenoghu bones (that someone else left from
fountain quaffing), and it occurred to me that while unlucky random is
unlucky, it shouldn't happen too far up in the dungeon.  For now it's a
flat chance; depending on some more thought, I may make the chance of
the demon lord/prince leaving vary in relation to how high up you are in
the dungeon.  (ie. Yeeny won't really want to stay around DL4, but DL38
is more entertaining)

This won't stop him from going through your bones and grabbing all the
good stuff, of course; the chance of him leaving is independent of that. ;)

> Does this include Juiblex and other homeless entities?  

All demon princes/demon lords, so yes.  "Home plane" here refers to
"whereever they came from", not "level they occupy in the dungeon."

> And if so, do items taken from the pile count as being in the game?  

Those items will be removed from the game prior to the bones save.

> homeless entity/level-specific monster be found carrying those
> acquired items when the hero finally summons them/arrives at their

No.  The items and the demon are just gone.  (If the demon will be
generated on a lower level, he will still be generated there.  If this
was the demon's lair and he hits the chance to 'leave', he will return 
to the downstairs where he normally waits, but he will not have the 
items with him.)  I may change this in the future, since it is fairly
easy to see if one of the four homed demons are on their own level, but
we'll see how it goes for the moment.

